Z||000006||Loki||06-12-2001||06:12 PM||||He posted on the fiero list...<BR>To Whom it May Concern,<BR>&gt; <BR>&gt; The time has come for me to post an official apology and Promise of Refund<BR>&gt; to <BR>&gt; any and all of my customers that either receieved their decals late or not<BR>&gt; at <BR>&gt; all.  I suppose that I was not ready to go into this business at all. I <BR>&gt; thought that I had a good idea, but lacked the planning to get the orders <BR>&gt; processed and shipped on time.  I lost many orders, some paid for, some<BR>&gt; not, <BR>&gt; in a giant paperwork fiasco and suffered numerous delays when the plotter <BR>&gt; used to make decals was made inaccessible to me for over a month.  The<BR>&gt; whole <BR>&gt; experience has been miserible for myself and I have disappointed most of<BR>&gt; you <BR>&gt; who decided to take a chance with me. For that, I am extremely embarrassed<BR>&gt; <BR>&gt; and offer a huge apology.<BR>&gt;     ANYONE who I owe money to is due a refund (some long overdue) and<BR>&gt; needs <BR>&gt; to mail me an official request with amount. I will add the 34 cents for <BR>&gt; postage to your refund if you want.  I do not want to get into trouble<BR>&gt; over <BR>&gt; the relatively samll total owed out. I have a wife and a baby coming and<BR>&gt; do <BR>&gt; not feel like I should go to jail or be harassed by the FBI. I am an<BR>&gt; honest <BR>&gt; man  who wants to make amends.  Please email me and I will get the address<BR>&gt; <BR>&gt; and specific info to you. I have already sent a few refunds and can<BR>&gt; provide <BR>&gt; you with references that I do pay back what I owe.<BR>&gt; <BR>&gt; Sincerely,<BR>&gt; Steve A. Wood<BR>&gt; Perseus Graphics (Defunct)<P><BR>He made  apublic apoligy and is trying to make amends......Give him an e-mail<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000007||Boomtastic||06-12-2001||07:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>He posted on the fiero list...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for posting that for me!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The email that got him back into the public spotlight was as follows:<P>"Steve Wood,<P>Due to your lack of response over the refund for decals that were never provided by you, I am notifying you that all information I have on you - your emails, email addresses, home address, telephone numbers, PayPal<BR>receipts, etc., as well as any other information that you may have defrauded anyone - will be turned over to the FBI's Task Force on Internet crime. I am sorry that it has come to this, but your lack of<BR>response to my repeated requests for a reimbursement have brought me to this. I will also be publicly (via any means that I can) encouraging anyone else that you have taken money from but have failed to provide a<BR>product to follow with their own FBI investigation.<P>Regards,<BR>Eric Schneck"<P> Since then, I have been in contact with Steve a few times, and he sounds as if he will be trying his best to pay each person back as he makes the money from his normal job. What this means is that everyone will get paid, but not at once as that would cause him to deplete his paycheck. Some would say "Too bad", but I think we should give him one last chance to make ammends. He has been made aware of the people that volalized their losses (and they have been cc'd the emails that have transpired between Steve and I), so I encourage each of you to hang in there, but do NOT give up the faith!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||MikeSchaefer||06-12-2001||09:47 PM||||I got three decals from him when he first started, really nice guy who wanted to start his own Fiero decal business, but I guess the funding was too much for him.  He's not the type of guy that should go to jail for something as petty as this.<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Loki||06-12-2001||11:58 PM||||Whats the amount people are out? Ive seen some say $8 some a bit more.. To me personally that doesnt warrent anything with the FBI for internet fruad....FBI may not even look at such a small amount form one person..But it depends on how many and the total..But he is trying to make amends and get the money out..Least he knows he made a mistake and got in over his head..More than alot of people will do..<P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000010||Songman||06-13-2001||02:59 AM||||I think Haze brought this up a while back. Did you ever get any response, decals, or refund, Carl?<P>From all that was written here a couple of months ago, the guy was working in a shop where he did vinyl signs or something. He came up with the idea that he could make some stuff for Fieros and maybe start his own business. Apparently, his boss didn't like the idea of him using the company's equipment to do this and he got fired. <P>I don't know how long all of this has been going on or if he will do anything, but I'd say as long as he is making an effort there is no reason to make more out of this than it really is. Nobody needs to go to jail as long as he handles the situation.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Boomtastic||06-13-2001||04:58 AM||||Yes, the amounts are relatively low, and yes, he is making an effort (finally) to repay the persons and clubs that he frauded. I agree - no one should (or will) be jailed for this, but sometimes the only way to get people to move is light the fire (or turn up the heat) under their butts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||SteveJ||06-13-2001||09:14 AM||||Just my opinion but I haven't seen anyone say they were actually repaid by this guy. Evidently he took all the money and converted it to his own uses and did not use it to produce product. His evident scheme to defraud his prior employer is disturbing as it reveals his business ethics.<BR>Most places have laws to handle this type of situation. Here in New York it is called a "Scheme to Defraud." It's a felony in which many people are defrauded out of small amounts the total of which is a felony amount.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Loki||06-13-2001||10:58 AM||||Several people have gotten there money back....ANd he just wants people to send in a confermation e-mail with the amount cause I belive he lost alot of the paper work....But People are getting money back<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
